cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  mindeye2-lora: Low-Rank Adaptation of MindEye2 for Data-Efficient
  fMRI-to-Image Decoding
message: If you use this software or its results, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Patric
    family-names: "[Surname]"
    # orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000
repository-code: "https://github.com/<user>/mindeye2-lora"
abstract: >-
  A controlled comparison of LoRA against full fine-tuning for adapting the
  shared-subject MindEye2 fMRI-to-image model to a held-out participant with one
  hour of scanning data. Six adaptation strategies across three seeds, with a
  pre-specified statistical analysis, on a single consumer GPU.
keywords:
  - fMRI decoding
  - image reconstruction
  - MindEye2
  - Natural Scenes Dataset
  - LoRA
  - parameter-efficient fine-tuning
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-09-18"
references:
  - type: conference-paper
    title: "MindEye2: Shared-Subject Models Enable fMRI-To-Image with 1 Hour of Data"
    authors:
      - family-names: Scotti
        given-names: Paul S.
      - name: "and others"
    collection-title: Proceedings of the 41st International Conference on Machine Learning
    year: 2024
    notes: The architecture, pretrained checkpoints and decoder used by this work.
  - type: article
    title: >-
      A massive 7T fMRI dataset to bridge cognitive neuroscience and artificial
      intelligence
    authors:
      - family-names: Allen
        given-names: Emily J.
      - name: "and others"
    journal: Nature Neuroscience
    year: 2022
    notes: The Natural Scenes Dataset, used under its own terms.
